sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Publisher as Publisher worker
    participant Store as Persistence outbox queries
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Kafka as Kafka topic

    loop Poll for next event
        Publisher->>Store: next_unpublished_event()
        Store->>DB: Select oldest unpublished row by sequence
        alt No event is available
            DB-->>Store: No row
            Store-->>Publisher: None
            Publisher->>Publisher: Wait 500 ms
        else Event found
            DB-->>Store: Event, target topic, key, payload, attempts
            Store-->>Publisher: Unpublished event
            Publisher->>Kafka: Send keyed event and wait for broker acknowledgement
            alt Kafka acknowledges
                Kafka-->>Publisher: Delivery acknowledgement
                Publisher->>Store: mark_outbox_event_published(event_id)
                Store->>DB: Set published_at and clear last_error
                DB-->>Store: Updated
                Store-->>Publisher: Published
            else Kafka delivery fails
                Kafka-->>Publisher: Delivery error or timeout
                Publisher->>Store: record_outbox_publish_failure(event_id, error)
                Store->>DB: Increment attempts and save bounded error
                DB-->>Store: Updated
                Store-->>Publisher: Failure recorded
                Publisher->>Publisher: Wait 2 seconds, then retry
            end
        end
    end
    Note over Publisher,DB: If Kafka accepts a message but the DB mark fails, the message can be sent again. Delivery is at least once.
